    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-12T04:11:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-12T04:11:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-11T18:41:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-11T18:41:00Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front crossing the eastern parts of SA will continue moving eastwards and cross the rest of the state early today. A ridge of high pressure will then push into SA from the west today, with the associated high moving over SA on Thursday. The high then gradually drifts southwards to be located in vicinity of Tasmania over the weekend, as it continues extending a ridge across SA.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-12T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-13T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-11T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-12T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Yunta, becoming less likely in the late morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm about the Gammon Ranges later tonight. Winds west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h tending south to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the morning and early afternoon then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 15 and 19.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:10am to 2:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-13T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-14T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-12T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-13T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning frost south of Leigh Creek. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then tending south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 3 and 6 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-14T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-15T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-13T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-14T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 23.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-15T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-14T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Yunta. Winds southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
